A||||12||CUTTER||Performance Chips?||||5
Z||000000||CUTTER||09-30-1999||10:39 PM||||What do you guys(and girls) think of the Performance chips in the Fiero store magizine? do they help performance alot? They run 150-200 bucks. I am thinking of getting one. and are they easy to put in? Which chip do you recommend for high porformance but not over 200 bucks?<p>[This message has been edited by CUTTER (edited 10-01-1999).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||mwbackus||09-30-1999||11:10 PM||||I would reccommend that you invest your dollar in some other proven performance modification, you may be much happier.  <BR>But, if I were to run an aftermarket chip, it would be the hypertech thermomaster, and only with the intention of gaining the low temp operation benefits from a 160 stat and 176 degree fan switch.  The Removal of the cat. converter and the use of higher octane fuel are both requirements for using this chip, and these drawbacks may actually outway any benefits realized from the low temp operation.  This is partly due to the fact that I live in an area with relatively strict I/M checks, so your situation may differ.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000002||fastonpumpgas||10-01-1999||10:03 PM||||MW is right it really doesnt make any sense to just put a chip ion with out doing it all, in essense what the chip does is makes your car run under 180 degrees which makes it think it is in a cool start condition, So it is like having the choke stuck open, So if you dont have proper flow to get all that extra gas true you really wont see alot of performance increases.  Plus it will ruin your gas milage. there are lots of things under 200 I would recomend, start with a 180 thermostat and maybe the 176 fan switch. I have heard the ignition is poor on the 2.8, that might be next.  and so far you are still under 100 bucks.   Ask what worked and what did, i rebuild lots of 350's, this is my first 2.8 so I really cant be much help, milling the heads might be the next option<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||CUTTER||10-01-1999||10:51 PM||||Acually it was the ADS performance chip in the Fiero Store Magazine. Its 80 bucks. Someone said I would have to get performance air filter and oil filter if I get the chip, like K&N. Is this true? and why?||||reg||1
Z||000004||88 Fiero||10-02-1999||12:57 AM||||Cutter...they just want to sell you this chips...If they do really work..I mean adds HP gains..Then a lot of guys won't be buying performance stuff for the engine and just settle for a chip to gain HP. I have a Customize Chip in my car where the Fuel Cut-Off has been eliminated, but I also have performance cam as well as the low temp thermostat and fan switch. and a custom air intake. I ran it always in high premium gas and did notice some horse power gain. I am ordering my Headers from FOCOA and will be hooking up a camaro 3.4 block. I also have the Miller Woods Turbo or you should say the Design One Turbo same guy who started this project. I paid only $1,000.00 for it includes everything I need. The good thing about the this Turbo unit is that the exhaust system is awesome. If you look the car in the rear you can see the 2 glass pack hanging and makes you wonder what it is...really neat package...So spend the money on some engine mods before you do the chip... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||10-02-1999||01:25 AM||||Does that turbo have a way of retarding the timing under boost conditions?||||reg||1
Z||000006||88 Fiero||10-02-1999||01:39 AM||||Tom..don't know much about turbo's...but I'll tell you what...I have a copy of the installation manuals of Design One Turbo/Miller Woods Turbo...from Stage 1 to Stage II Unit...It illustrates the installation process of their unit and the things that comes with the Turbo package..very interesting...||||reg||1
