Z||000008||terryk||10-02-1999||09:31 AM||||GM does a damn good job of tuning the engines. There is not that much performance to gain from chips (except on turbo cars where you can crank up the boost). Some of the early chips were pure theft (email me for details if you care). They remove the limiters, add some timing (which helps a bit), but some add fuel which is not good. See my comments on AE vs PE. Cruise EGR gets changed, but I think that is not good either. The 660 engine likes to ping in the 2800 RPM range.<P>The 6869 ECM supports a turbo (wastegate) if the quad driver is added to the circuit board and the feature is enabled in the chip. The 7170 is the same circuit board, but doesn't support the wastegate because they remove the code from the embedded processor rom (the calibration tables are in the eprom with some application specific code whereas the the main program code is in the embedded processor rom).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||88 Fiero||10-02-1999||11:41 AM||||Greg...I got the Turbo which was the made by Kevin of Design One/Miller Woods thru my friend Keith of Fiero Motorsports. He has this turbo for a while and he is not interested in hooking it up to his car because he got his Northstar engine and working on it. I figure since he's not going to used it I ask him how much he would sell the Turbo unit and he said $1,000.00 plus we've been friends for more than 10 yrs....All I need now is order the Stage II from Kevin (Design One)but have to pay the price of $800.00....{=o)||||reg||1
